# The train fought many times, so that a change to the board shows up here as well as in the
# tests. A bot that could not summon, or that stalled when a floor filled up and a card stopped
# doing anything, would fail this.
#
# Both bots win every run of all three fights. That is not a measurement of the content: three
# small fights against enemies with one move each are winnable, and a level is a fact about the
# bot rather than about the cards. What this is for is the two expectations at the bottom: that
# nothing throws, and that no run stalls. The hp column is the part worth reading, and it climbs
# from 0.6 to 13.4 across the three as the Brood Mother fills her floor.
#
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Cantrip.Cli -- sim samples/board

scenario "Climbing the train"
  runs 200

  player hp 40
  player energy 3
  deck 4 "Summon Imp", 3 Pike, 2 "Post a Sentinel", 2 Sweep

  battle Crawler
  battle Crawler, Crawler
  battle "Brood Mother", Crawler

  expect no stalls
  expect no errors
